Implements real-time score tracking for captured pieces using standard chess values (♙=1, ♞♝=3, ♜=5, ♛=9).

## Backend Changes

- **ChessBoard**: Added `m_whiteScore`/`m_blackScore` members with `getPieceValue()` helper
- **movePiece()**: Tracks captured piece type before board update, increments scorer's total
- Handles en passant correctly by detecting pawn capture before removal

```cpp
// Capture tracking before piece removal
PieceType capturedPieceType = PieceType::None;
if (isCapture && !isEnPassant) {
    capturedPieceType = m_board[to.y()][to.x()].getType();
} else if (isEnPassant) {
    capturedPieceType = PieceType::Pawn;
}

// Score update after move execution
if (capturedPieceType != PieceType::None) {
    int pieceValue = getPieceValue(capturedPieceType);
    if (pieceColor == PieceColor::White) {
        m_whiteScore += pieceValue;
    } else {
        m_blackScore += pieceValue;
    }
}
```

## Frontend Changes

- **Qt_Chess**: Added "吃子分數" group box above time controls with score labels
- **updateBoard()**: Calls `updateScoreDisplay()` to sync UI with game state
- Scores auto-reset on `initializeBoard()`

